# 6.2.referral.yield.patient.stone

## .what

write the **patient layer** — the plain-language summary a layperson reads: "here's who to see and
how to get seen." this is the **interface** on top of the clinical engine (6.1). the raw rank and
citations sit beneath; the patient is never handed a raw list to self-interpret.

## .inputs

- `6.1.referral.yield.clinical.yield.md` — the full clinical detail (the engine to translate)

## .do

- translate the top-ranked options into plain language: who to see, the venue (virtual or in-person),
  and how to get seen (the walkable path — open-this-week vs covered-but-waits)
- state the **given urgency** in plain words, exactly as the diagnostician set it — do not soften or
  sharpen it (a "soon" stays "soon", not re-judged into "whenever")
- point to the preparation sheet in plain terms (what to carry, what to ask)
- carry the **not-medical-advice disclaimer** — this output is read by a layperson and acted on
- add the **emergency carve-out**: if the case reads as an emergency, say plainly "call your local
  emergency number now" (per `motto.not-medical-advice`)

## .emit

into `6.2.referral.yield.patient.yield.md` — the plain-language summary, disclaimer + emergency
carve-out attached.

## .done when

the plain-language "who to see and how to get seen" summary is written, the given urgency is stated
unaltered, the not-medical-advice disclaimer is present, and the emergency carve-out is included.
